WEBVTT

00:00.780 --> 00:03.850
I'm trying to wash my T-shirts...

00:04.170 --> 00:06.770
so why are your socks in here?!

00:06.770 --> 00:10.080
Are you totally dumb?
Now I have to start all over!

00:10.080 --> 00:13.030
What's it matter?
They'll get clean either way!

00:13.030 --> 00:16.030
Utilities

00:13.030 --> 00:16.030
Electric

00:13.030 --> 00:16.030
Water

00:13.030 --> 00:16.030
Gas

00:13.030 --> 00:16.030
yen

00:13.030 --> 00:17.320
If we wash everyone's loads separately,
it adds to the water and electric bills!

00:17.740 --> 00:19.850
No way. That's gross.

00:20.370 --> 00:23.580
What if your weird fluids
soak into my shirts?

00:23.580 --> 00:25.850
I don't have any weird fluids!

00:25.850 --> 00:29.530
You do, too! They're coming
from you all the time!

00:30.650 --> 00:34.010
What? I need to get along better with Ouka?

00:34.010 --> 00:37.390
Yeah. You gotta stop fighting all the time.

00:37.390 --> 00:41.370
Screw that. She's the one getting
on my case over every little thing.

00:41.370 --> 00:42.890
Look...

00:42.890 --> 00:46.000
Do you think anyone will want
to be in a café where the owner

00:46.000 --> 00:47.650
and employees don't get along?

00:47.650 --> 00:49.140
If you're gonna hire people,

00:49.140 --> 00:52.840
put in the effort to create
a comfortable working environment.

00:55.140 --> 00:59.130
Who was it that said he'd bow his head
if it'd help the business?

00:59.130 --> 01:02.410
I... did say that, but...

01:02.410 --> 01:05.350
Quit looking at porn sites in broad daylight,

01:05.350 --> 01:07.870
and go make amends with Ouka-chan.

01:06.670 --> 01:09.290
Volume

01:07.870 --> 01:08.950
What?!

01:09.290 --> 01:11.780
I'm not looking at porn sites!

01:10.710 --> 01:13.010
Opening Soon

01:29.060 --> 01:31.650
The Café Terrace and Its Goddesses

02:45.320 --> 02:48.890
It's so nice out.
The clothes should be dry in no time.

02:45.390 --> 02:48.890
Episode 3: "Opening!"

02:50.790 --> 02:51.940
She's right.

02:52.220 --> 02:55.940
I do need to build positive
relationships with them.

02:56.900 --> 02:57.940
Come on!

02:57.940 --> 03:00.300
It's got your weird fluids in it!

03:00.300 --> 03:01.420
Hey!

03:02.620 --> 03:07.580
Worst café ever

03:02.620 --> 03:07.580
The secret ingredient is the pervy owner's fluids

03:02.810 --> 03:07.130
If the female customers hear her say
something like that, they'll never come back.

03:08.030 --> 03:10.920
How am I supposed to get
along with her, though?

03:11.460 --> 03:14.110
It's like taming a wild beast.

03:14.110 --> 03:16.120
Why don't you just compliment her?

03:18.040 --> 03:19.610
Where'd you come from?!

03:19.610 --> 03:21.340
She's an open book.

03:21.820 --> 03:24.080
And you're good at that kinda thing, right?

03:24.080 --> 03:26.760
Just keep telling her she's cute.

03:26.760 --> 03:27.860
Huh?

03:28.350 --> 03:33.020
Spare me that nonsense.
It didn't work at all on you.

03:34.950 --> 03:36.020
Well, I'm...

03:36.520 --> 03:38.300
kinda used to hearing it.

03:41.440 --> 03:45.320
Hey, what's wrong, Akane-san?
Your face is red.

03:45.320 --> 03:48.460
Jeez... I'm gonna have some coffee.

03:50.240 --> 03:51.540
Hey!

03:52.370 --> 03:55.250
What are you doing just standing there?

03:55.600 --> 03:57.960
If you're bored,
get the café ready for opening.

03:59.120 --> 04:01.770
Just shut up! I don't need that from—

04:02.720 --> 04:05.790
Whoops... I can't do that.

04:05.790 --> 04:07.680
Gotta smile...

04:07.680 --> 04:13.100
Y-You said you hate cleaning,
but you're proactive about doing laundry.

04:13.100 --> 04:15.750
That's pretty admirable, for you.

04:21.440 --> 04:24.490
What's with that face?! It's pissing me off!

04:24.490 --> 04:26.480
I was giving you a compliment!

04:26.480 --> 04:27.240
What?!

04:27.580 --> 04:30.220
That was just a roundabout
way of insulting me!

04:30.220 --> 04:32.000
Also, you're being creepy!

04:32.000 --> 04:35.000
Don't skulk around here
when I'm doing my laundry!

04:32.000 --> 04:35.000
What? They're fighting again?

04:35.000 --> 04:39.100
They really hate each other's guts, huh?
Like a horse and a deer.

04:39.100 --> 04:40.630
I'd say a dog and a monkey.

04:40.630 --> 04:45.470
What do you mean, "creepy"?!
Just take the compliment!

04:40.940 --> 04:45.470
I don't think Hayato-kun is
really such a bad guy, though.

04:45.470 --> 04:48.680
Yeah! He's just a little perverted!

04:45.470 --> 04:49.770
I'm busy here! What are you
doing over there, anyway?

04:48.680 --> 04:50.560
Not as much as you, though!

04:49.770 --> 04:51.130
I'm, uh...

04:50.560 --> 04:51.450
Huh?

04:51.450 --> 04:54.170
I said, "Not as much as you, though!"

04:54.170 --> 04:55.000
Huh?

04:57.990 --> 05:01.190
Insults come out so easily, and yet...

05:02.820 --> 05:05.200
Her dinner was awful again, too.

05:09.680 --> 05:12.260
It's all pretty good, except this salad!

05:12.790 --> 05:16.440
Well, excuse <i>me</i>! I made the salad!

05:16.440 --> 05:17.590
On the nose!

05:18.170 --> 05:23.130
Who puts actual wine on salad
instead of wine vinegar?

05:23.560 --> 05:26.520
What am I even supposed to compliment?

05:28.450 --> 05:30.270
Hey, Hayato-kun.

05:31.140 --> 05:33.990
Could you tell Ouka-chan the bath's free?

05:34.520 --> 05:35.390
Sure.

05:36.340 --> 05:40.150
Hey, Ouka. The bath's free.

05:40.150 --> 05:41.260
Hey...

05:42.160 --> 05:43.480
Are you listening?

05:43.480 --> 05:46.230
At least answer... me...

05:50.440 --> 05:52.890
Hey! Don't just barge in here!

05:52.890 --> 05:54.750
But... what are you doing?

05:54.750 --> 05:57.870
What does it matter? Leave me alone!

05:57.870 --> 06:00.600
We can't work in clothes that are
hard to move around in,

06:00.600 --> 06:02.650
so I was just giving it one more check.

06:03.130 --> 06:07.610
Wait... You're gonna show up
at the café in that?

06:07.610 --> 06:09.260
The other four are, too!

06:09.260 --> 06:11.720
Even Grandma was on board with it!

06:11.720 --> 06:13.010
She said it was cute!

06:13.010 --> 06:14.260
You got a problem with it?

06:15.890 --> 06:18.020
Eh, it's fine, I guess.

06:18.020 --> 06:18.780
Huh?

06:18.780 --> 06:22.060
It does make you look somewhat better.

06:22.400 --> 06:25.780
Huh?! What's that supposed to mean?!
Are you making fun of me?!

06:26.340 --> 06:28.110
Oh, crap...

06:28.110 --> 06:35.120
I-I'm saying even someone as unhinged
as you can look fairly cute in that.

06:35.120 --> 06:38.620
We might get more customers who just
come to see the uniforms, you know?

06:38.620 --> 06:40.270
So, I mean... What I'm saying is...

06:40.270 --> 06:44.140
You get two thumbs up from me!
At least, as far as the uniform goes!

06:44.140 --> 06:47.210
I screwed up! That was
basically just insulting her!

06:47.210 --> 06:50.930
But other than that,
what is there to compliment?!

06:54.530 --> 06:57.430
That's so nice. Thank you.

06:58.350 --> 06:59.140
Huh?

06:59.140 --> 07:04.190
But... I was complimenting
the uniform, not you.

07:04.190 --> 07:07.210
I know. That's why I'm thanking you.

07:07.210 --> 07:08.110
Huh?

07:09.680 --> 07:11.270
I mean, because...

07:12.760 --> 07:14.800
I made these uniforms.

07:14.800 --> 07:16.580
Y-You did?

07:18.430 --> 07:22.110
The tech school I go to is a fashion school.

07:22.110 --> 07:25.380
I'm hoping to be a costume designer someday.

07:25.380 --> 07:28.130
Oh... I had no idea.

07:28.480 --> 07:30.380
Grandma told me...

07:31.060 --> 07:35.480
Hayato may be sharp-tongued and defiant,

07:35.480 --> 07:38.420
but the one thing he never did was lie.

07:40.260 --> 07:43.260
So I'm really happy!

07:44.440 --> 07:46.480
All of these girls

07:46.480 --> 07:49.870
just believed everything Grandma said
like it was gospel, huh?

07:49.870 --> 07:53.990
Oh... I think your coffee
has gotten a lot better, too.

07:54.880 --> 07:55.740
You do?

07:55.740 --> 07:58.370
Yeah. It actually has some aroma now.

07:58.920 --> 08:02.120
Wow, really? It has aroma now?!

08:03.520 --> 08:06.000
I'm not smelling any aroma from you, though.

08:06.440 --> 08:10.010
You're not allowed to take any baths
for the next few days.

08:10.480 --> 08:11.560
What the—

08:12.360 --> 08:13.880
Wait! Did she get like this...

08:14.790 --> 08:17.470
just from the wine on that salad?!

08:20.850 --> 08:23.610
Hey! Why are you taking pictures, Ami-chan?!

08:23.610 --> 08:24.230
Huh?

08:24.230 --> 08:26.760
So I have proof that
Shiragiku-san's a pervert!

08:26.760 --> 08:28.270
Well, stop!

08:28.270 --> 08:31.280
And Hayato-kun, stop smirking! It's creepy!

08:31.280 --> 08:32.890
I'm not smirking!

08:38.720 --> 08:41.960
Hayacchi! Whatcha doin'?

08:42.660 --> 08:44.920
Hello? You listening?

08:46.880 --> 08:49.360
So, Hayacchi, what're you doing, huh?

08:49.360 --> 08:51.420
Huh? Huh? Huh?!

08:51.720 --> 08:53.100
Shut up!

08:53.100 --> 08:55.210
If you've got time to play with dumbbells,

08:55.210 --> 08:57.040
go make some coffee or something!

08:58.290 --> 08:59.560
I swear...

08:59.560 --> 09:01.060
Hayato-kun?

09:01.060 --> 09:02.810
We should get going.

09:02.810 --> 09:04.240
Oh, right.

09:04.240 --> 09:05.560
Coming.

09:10.630 --> 09:16.340
Shiragiku and I went out to visit
some of our regulars earlier.

09:17.160 --> 09:21.120
We'll finally be ready to reopen
Café Terrace Familia tomorrow.

09:21.470 --> 09:22.810
It's finally time!

09:22.810 --> 09:24.790
We should celebrate tonight!

09:25.720 --> 09:28.380
I'll make a feast.
Oh, and I'll get us alcohol!

09:28.380 --> 09:29.500
Please don't.

09:30.620 --> 09:33.800
All we can do now is pray
that people will come.

09:33.800 --> 09:37.970
It'll be fine. We've got the uniforms
you had so much praise for.

09:37.970 --> 09:42.600
Yeah, and you <i>have</i> gotten a little
better at making coffee, Hayato.

09:42.600 --> 09:46.350
It's all happening because you
had the will to make it happen.

09:46.350 --> 09:51.110
I'm still worried, though. Our Master doesn't
seem like he'll be great with customers.

09:53.110 --> 09:57.020
Huh? What's wrong, Ami-chan?
You're being awfully quiet.

09:57.020 --> 09:57.660
Huh?

09:57.660 --> 10:00.370
You're usually the one making the most noise.

10:02.120 --> 10:06.190
Oh, yeah! We finally get to reopen! Yay!

10:06.190 --> 10:07.000
Little late...

10:07.000 --> 10:09.050
I don't get you at all.

10:09.480 --> 10:11.000
Oh, right.

10:11.080 --> 10:14.460
Tsuruga Ami

10:11.760 --> 10:14.460
It's not much, but here's
your pay for last month.

10:14.800 --> 10:15.820
Huh?

10:16.270 --> 10:18.180
That's great, but are you sure it's okay?

10:18.180 --> 10:21.390
You don't have that much
saved up either, do you?

10:21.390 --> 10:25.140
You don't have to put on a show.
It can wait until after we open.

10:26.020 --> 10:29.690
How very naïve.
As sweet as the café au lait you make.

10:29.690 --> 10:30.490
Huh?

10:31.230 --> 10:34.010
I'll have you know the stocks
I've been dabbling in

10:34.010 --> 10:36.110
since high school have been rising of late.

10:36.110 --> 10:38.410
Stocks? Since high school?

10:38.410 --> 10:39.820
I think I hate him.

10:39.820 --> 10:42.490
That'll make things easier for us, though.

10:42.490 --> 10:46.700
I see. That explains why you seemed
to lack any sense of urgency.

10:47.370 --> 10:51.670
Tsukishima Riho

10:47.710 --> 10:50.430
In that case, I'm happy to accept mine...

10:50.430 --> 10:52.560
before all those stocks tank.

10:51.670 --> 10:53.960
Tsukishima Riho

10:52.560 --> 10:54.750
Cut it out! You'll jinx it!

10:55.050 --> 10:57.390
Wait... Only 20,000 yen? Seriously?

10:57.390 --> 10:59.470
That's on the high end for you!

11:00.450 --> 11:02.320
It's just about time.

11:02.320 --> 11:06.220
I'm glad they've all been able to
mesh with me so quickly, though.

11:06.680 --> 11:08.910
If we were all still hostile,

11:08.910 --> 11:11.480
there's no way we could keep
a café running together.

11:14.970 --> 11:16.480
Why do you think it is?

11:18.000 --> 11:20.360
How long have you been there?!

11:20.830 --> 11:22.170
Why do you think it is?

11:22.170 --> 11:24.240
Huh? Why what is?

11:24.810 --> 11:28.780
Why we were all able to
mesh with you so quickly.

11:30.040 --> 11:34.140
Think about it. Who do you think
we should thank for that?

11:34.560 --> 11:35.500
Who?

11:35.880 --> 11:38.300
The reason we could accept you
so soon after we first met,

11:38.300 --> 11:40.510
as if we'd already known you for a long time,

11:40.940 --> 11:43.700
as if we were already family...

11:44.590 --> 11:45.750
What is it?

11:47.140 --> 11:49.050
Your grandma told us about you.

11:49.050 --> 11:51.560
She said she had a grandson
who got into Tokyo U.

11:51.560 --> 11:53.400
She said it was her grandson's favorite,

11:53.400 --> 11:57.820
so she wanted me to make it for him
if anything happened to her.

11:57.820 --> 12:01.020
It was the one promise we made with Grandma!

12:01.690 --> 12:05.060
That we'd always eat our meals
together, as a family.

12:07.310 --> 12:08.420
I see.

12:09.720 --> 12:11.310
It was Grandma.

12:11.310 --> 12:15.550
Maybe she told them all those things
because she thought

12:15.550 --> 12:18.840
she might not be here anymore
when I came back.

12:21.160 --> 12:23.150
Looks like you get it now.

12:23.150 --> 12:24.180
Yeah.

12:24.690 --> 12:26.540
Thanks to you.

12:27.720 --> 12:31.860
I thought she was stupid,
but she's actually...

12:34.440 --> 12:35.540
That's right!

12:37.210 --> 12:39.780
It was all thanks to me!

12:40.690 --> 12:41.680
What?

12:41.680 --> 12:43.070
I <i>said</i>...

12:43.070 --> 12:44.200
No, I heard you.

12:44.570 --> 12:46.800
Man, it was hard work, too!

12:46.800 --> 12:49.370
You're so quick to start fights!

12:49.370 --> 12:54.290
Where would we be if you didn't have
a calming influence like me around?

12:54.290 --> 12:57.790
Nope, I was right. She's an idiot!

12:58.220 --> 12:59.540
Are you grateful?

12:59.900 --> 13:01.510
Yep. Sure am.

13:01.510 --> 13:02.810
Are you really?

13:02.810 --> 13:06.550
It's thanks to me
that we're all like family now!

13:06.550 --> 13:08.760
I know, I know.

13:10.870 --> 13:14.020
Well, good, then! Guess I'll head back now!

13:14.800 --> 13:16.730
Well, whatever.

13:20.240 --> 13:22.580
What? Weren't you heading back?

13:23.400 --> 13:24.440
But you know...

13:25.180 --> 13:29.320
The things that are precious to you
are more easily broken than you'd think.

13:30.360 --> 13:33.370
If that which is most precious
to you breaks someday

13:33.660 --> 13:37.830
and it's my fault... I'm sorry.

13:39.190 --> 13:41.590
What... does that mean?

13:45.780 --> 13:46.840
Huh?

13:46.840 --> 13:50.060
Wh-Why are my phone and laptop broken?

13:50.550 --> 13:53.010
Yeah, uh...

13:53.520 --> 13:58.020
I went to make tea
like you told me to, and...

13:58.020 --> 14:00.000
Boom!

13:58.020 --> 14:00.980
Boom!

14:00.000 --> 14:01.820
Watch it, Ami-chan.

14:01.820 --> 14:05.020
It's dangerous to carry tea
and dumbbells at the same time.

14:05.020 --> 14:07.820
No problem! I've been
building up my finger strength!

14:08.030 --> 14:10.240
BOOM

14:08.270 --> 14:09.370
Yah!

14:11.190 --> 14:12.370
Ah!

14:12.930 --> 14:14.370
Aaaah!

14:17.620 --> 14:21.000
Why would you keep holding
your dumbbells while serving tea?!

14:24.550 --> 14:25.850
I get it now!

14:25.850 --> 14:29.260
That's why you were so quiet
when we were eating lunch!

14:29.260 --> 14:31.610
Um, Hayato-kun...

14:31.610 --> 14:32.600
What?!

14:32.600 --> 14:36.590
The company that you said
you bought stocks in

14:36.590 --> 14:39.640
was in some major scandal, and it
looks like they're going bankrupt.

14:39.640 --> 14:41.080
It was just on the news...

14:41.800 --> 14:42.860
For real?!

14:42.860 --> 14:45.070
I gotta sell right away!

14:47.530 --> 14:53.580
B-But you bought stocks in multiple
companies to minimize risk, right?

14:54.120 --> 14:59.370
I did, but I moved them all to this company
because this café was do-or-die...

15:00.520 --> 15:01.880
You mean...

15:01.880 --> 15:06.340
If I don't sell right now, these stocks
will be nothing but scrap paper!

15:07.080 --> 15:11.460
Easy, there! For now,
wanna give 'em a squeeze?

15:11.840 --> 15:14.480
I have <i>had</i> it with you!

15:14.480 --> 15:18.240
I <i>told</i> you the most precious
things are easily broken!

15:18.240 --> 15:22.010
And so, after hitting limit down on my stocks
reduced my savings to basically zero,

15:22.010 --> 15:24.660
Café Terrace Familia finally reopened.

15:24.660 --> 15:27.980
But I apologized!

15:29.380 --> 15:33.120
As a rule, we'll have just two
part-timers working at once,

15:33.120 --> 15:35.240
but this is our first day.

15:35.240 --> 15:39.800
Plus, having all five of you in those
uniforms will have a bigger impact.

15:39.800 --> 15:42.500
Just be honest and say we look pretty.

15:42.500 --> 15:44.260
Oh, shut up.

15:44.820 --> 15:45.960
Anyway...

15:46.400 --> 15:50.550
For various reasons,
this café has zero funds right now.

15:50.550 --> 15:51.680
So...

15:51.930 --> 15:54.190
Stay focused, all of you!

15:54.190 --> 15:57.680
As of today, Café Terrace Familia
is back in business!

15:58.080 --> 15:59.030
Right!

16:00.350 --> 16:02.810
Oh, here, Akane-chan.

16:03.330 --> 16:05.310
You need to do all the buttons.

16:05.310 --> 16:08.040
It's only cute when you wear it right.

16:08.040 --> 16:10.450
It's too tight around my neck, though.

16:10.450 --> 16:13.360
Hey, that actually looks good on you.

16:13.360 --> 16:17.020
You kinda look like some rich young lady.

16:21.640 --> 16:22.830
Well, thanks.

16:23.330 --> 16:25.580
Hey! What are you doing?!

16:27.210 --> 16:28.550
I swear...

16:28.840 --> 16:31.420
Seriously, I need you guys to stay focused.

16:31.420 --> 16:34.590
And we need <i>you</i> to stay focused, Hayato-kun.

16:34.590 --> 16:35.300
Huh?

16:35.300 --> 16:39.680
Not everyone who comes
to this café is going to be a nice person.

16:39.680 --> 16:42.810
You can't lose your temper
or lash out at people over just anything.

16:43.840 --> 16:46.110
If anyone gets too nasty,

16:46.110 --> 16:49.980
just politely ask them to leave. Got it?

16:49.980 --> 16:53.210
Yes, I know. Don't treat me like a child.

16:53.210 --> 16:56.610
Also, I'm not the type to hit people.

16:56.610 --> 16:58.040
You sure about that?

16:58.040 --> 17:01.070
I guess if it comes to it,
Ami-chan and I will have to stop you.

17:01.070 --> 17:02.080
Yep!

17:02.080 --> 17:04.380
I told you, I won't do anything.

17:05.580 --> 17:07.820
Wow, I guess this café reopened.

17:07.820 --> 17:08.730
Yeah.

17:08.730 --> 17:10.460
Come on in!

17:10.460 --> 17:13.380
Welcome to Café Terrace Familia!

17:14.830 --> 17:16.810
Please have a seat here.

17:17.750 --> 17:21.240
It all starts now... Finally.

17:21.680 --> 17:24.540
I see the waitresses have new uniforms.

17:24.540 --> 17:26.810
Yes! I made them!

17:27.160 --> 17:29.560
What can I get for you?

17:30.850 --> 17:32.840
Two house blends!

17:43.120 --> 17:44.860
Thank you for waiting.

17:45.770 --> 17:46.950
Your blend coffee.

17:58.760 --> 18:00.960
This is pretty good.

18:00.960 --> 18:04.060
It tastes almost exactly the same
as the previous owner's coffee.

18:05.480 --> 18:07.400
It smells great, too.

18:07.400 --> 18:09.190
Um, um...

18:09.190 --> 18:13.880
This coffee was made by
the previous owner's grandson.

18:14.320 --> 18:18.030
Oh, I see! We'll be stopping by again.

18:18.930 --> 18:20.530
Thank you!

18:20.530 --> 18:23.660
Good for you. They complimented your coffee.

18:23.660 --> 18:25.660
Shut up. Get to work.

18:27.410 --> 18:30.030
We came straight over to drink your coffee!

18:30.030 --> 18:31.960
Congratulations on your opening!

18:31.960 --> 18:33.370
Welcome!

18:42.220 --> 18:44.800
It's going well, isn't it, Hayato-kun?

18:44.800 --> 18:45.830
I guess so.

18:46.930 --> 18:48.310
Welcome.

18:49.000 --> 18:50.060
Oh...

18:50.480 --> 18:53.500
So this café really did reopen, eh?

18:53.500 --> 18:56.820
I thought it had shut down
after the old lady died.

18:58.370 --> 18:59.450
He's...

18:59.910 --> 19:03.580
You're killing me here.
Didn't you promise it by today?

19:03.580 --> 19:06.450
I'm sorry! I'm truly sorry!

19:06.450 --> 19:10.460
I told you that old people can't run cafés.

19:10.460 --> 19:13.080
Just sell this dumb place already.

19:13.710 --> 19:16.710
Uh... Please have a seat here.

19:17.910 --> 19:21.180
You! Bring me your most expensive coffee!

19:21.180 --> 19:23.770
O-Okay. Um—

19:23.770 --> 19:24.930
I heard him.

19:25.330 --> 19:26.510
He's...

19:26.510 --> 19:29.270
The guy who always
came here to hassle Grandma.

19:29.270 --> 19:30.880
This isn't good.

19:30.880 --> 19:32.980
Y-Yeah...

19:34.810 --> 19:38.380
You there! Are you her
grandson, by any chance?

19:38.380 --> 19:40.350
The old lady's grandson?

19:40.350 --> 19:41.200
Yes.

19:41.650 --> 19:42.780
Ami-chan...

19:43.320 --> 19:47.200
I know. If Hayacchi does
anything funny, I'll run right over.

19:47.200 --> 19:50.750
Oh, I see! So you took over the business!

19:50.750 --> 19:53.210
Come over here. Let me see your face.

19:53.210 --> 19:55.170
I saved her skin.

19:55.450 --> 19:59.510
Fuwa-san, I appreciate
what you did back then.

19:59.820 --> 20:03.510
My grandmother was able to keep
the café running thanks to you.

20:04.290 --> 20:06.430
Hey. Shouldn't you be bowing?

20:07.850 --> 20:12.090
If you appreciate what I did,
the first thing you should do is bow.

20:12.090 --> 20:14.980
Go on, bow. Just like your grandma did.

20:14.980 --> 20:18.970
Who do you think made it possible
for you to grow up big and strong?

20:18.970 --> 20:20.070
Well?!

20:21.920 --> 20:23.240
Hayato-kun!

20:26.920 --> 20:28.840
Thank you very much.

20:31.580 --> 20:34.790
Hmph. Your posture needs work.

20:35.420 --> 20:38.540
Your grandma was a lot better at it.

20:38.540 --> 20:43.320
She'd bow at a perfect 45 degrees,
her back straight as an arrow.

20:43.320 --> 20:46.010
There's no pleasure in it for me
if you don't do the same.

20:46.460 --> 20:50.250
Whenever I called out to her on
the street, she'd rush right over.

20:50.250 --> 20:52.880
And she always greeted me properly,

20:52.880 --> 20:56.680
bobbing her head up and down
like a Chinese grasshopper!

20:57.020 --> 20:58.800
Oh, do you know about those?

20:58.800 --> 21:01.980
When you grab a Chinese
grasshopper by the legs...

21:01.980 --> 21:04.530
they bob up and down like this!

21:04.840 --> 21:07.530
That's exactly what she looked like!

21:07.920 --> 21:12.540
Her bowing might have been
even better than her coffee.

21:12.540 --> 21:15.500
It's a shame I won't ever see it again.

21:16.030 --> 21:19.750
I sure wish she'd lived a little longer.

21:20.340 --> 21:24.490
All of our customers at this café
will be our familia,

21:24.490 --> 21:27.460
meaning they'll be part of
the Kasukabe family.

21:34.520 --> 21:35.690
Don't!

21:36.920 --> 21:38.020
Wha—

21:38.870 --> 21:40.230
I apologize.

21:40.540 --> 21:43.660
We've had a cockroach
running around since this morning,

21:43.660 --> 21:45.940
and I think it was sitting near your feet.

21:46.360 --> 21:48.080
A cockroach?

21:48.080 --> 21:50.410
All this ruckus at a business
where people eat?

21:50.410 --> 21:53.200
Can't you even keep
your part-timers in line?!

21:54.300 --> 21:57.050
And you put them in these sleazy uniforms?!

21:57.050 --> 21:58.210
What is this, a brothel?!

22:00.410 --> 22:01.080
Hey!

22:02.200 --> 22:04.380
S-Stop it! That hurts!

22:04.660 --> 22:09.040
Could I kindly ask you to leave
before I change my mind, old man?

22:09.040 --> 22:13.030
Go now, and I won't sue you
for sexual harassment.

22:14.730 --> 22:17.080
Ooh, a trial?!

22:17.080 --> 22:20.970
Go for it! We'll be your witnesses!

22:22.470 --> 22:23.520
Let go of me!

22:24.040 --> 22:25.840
Don't think this is over, boy!

22:26.820 --> 22:28.230
Come again.

22:28.230 --> 22:30.380
Um, Hayato-kun...

22:30.380 --> 22:33.850
Sorry about that.
I really wanted to deck him.

22:33.850 --> 22:37.460
Huh?! No, it's okay! Thank you!

22:37.460 --> 22:39.710
Go toss some salt around the entrance.

22:39.710 --> 22:42.000
We don't need bad omens on our first day.

22:42.000 --> 22:44.040
Right, Master!

22:44.040 --> 22:45.550
And be generous with it.

22:45.870 --> 22:49.620
Sorry for losing my cool after
lecturing you earlier and everything.

22:50.360 --> 22:54.470
I think it'd be more pathetic to do nothing
after being talked to like that.

22:54.930 --> 22:59.140
No, I get it now. I can see your resolve.

22:59.520 --> 23:01.080
Also, Akane...

23:01.080 --> 23:03.560
No hitting with mops. That's not even funny.

23:04.700 --> 23:07.070
Right. I'll be careful.

23:08.310 --> 23:10.200
That was so cool, Hayacchi!

23:10.200 --> 23:12.630
I'll help you out next time!

23:13.070 --> 23:17.370
Please don't! If you get involved,
we're definitely losing in court!

23:17.370 --> 23:19.160
Hey, Hayato-kun!

23:19.870 --> 23:23.560
You got pissed off when he badmouthed
our uniforms too, didn't you?

23:23.560 --> 23:24.460
Well?!

23:24.460 --> 23:27.710
Huh? Yeah... of course.

23:27.710 --> 23:29.140
Okay, then.

23:32.260 --> 23:34.890
I hope it's okay to use coarse salt...

23:33.390 --> 23:34.890
Coarse Salt

23:36.290 --> 23:41.460
Anyway, Hayato-kun really
hasn't changed at all in fifteen years.

23:42.020 --> 23:57.030
Episode 4: "Cherry Blossom Festival!"

23:42.580 --> 23:45.190
I'm sorry, Hayacchi! I'll pay for the laptop!

23:45.190 --> 23:47.660
How many months
would that take with your pay?

23:47.660 --> 23:51.260
It's okay! I got an email from a widow whose
husband was killed by a giant stag beetle,

23:51.260 --> 23:52.700
and she says she'll send me money if I reply!

23:52.700 --> 23:54.240
That's a spam message!

23:54.240 --> 23:56.450
I'll send it from your laptop!
